<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles Lawrence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1709">1709</a>–<a href="/years/1760">1760</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles Lawrence was a British army officer and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a> from 1753. Doubting the loyalty of the French-speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadians">Acadians</a>, he and his council ordered their <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> in 1755, expelling thousands to the British colonies and beyond. He then invited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-england">New England</a> Planters to settle their lands, and in 1758 called Nova Scotia's first elected assembly.</p></div>
